  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Responsive Stabilisation Through Transition (RESET)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Outcome 1: ongoing conflict analysis and monitoring will inform project prioritisation and adaptation and conflict sensitivity. Outcome 2: training and application builds capacity of existing peace and development structures, law enforcement, state and non-state actors&#x2019; to implement effective and sustainable conflict management responses and engage in inclusive community dialogue forums. Outcome 3: through democratic dialogues and co-designed stability workstreams communities and local authorities will strengthen local security and justice governance accountability and responsiveness including on land conflict. Outcome 4:  through reintegration activities, marginalised groups and ex-combatants will benefit from socio-economic opportunities.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RESET generates mutually reinforcing improvements in target communities&#x2019; social cohesion and their social contract with the state as key foundations of improved peace and stability. To accomplish this, RESET builds state and non-state actors&#x2019; and institutions&#x2019; ability to understand and anticipate outbreaks of conflict and implement conflict management responses towards two strategic outcomes, 1) increase community resilience to conflict and 2) strengthen trust and accountability between state and society.</narrative>
  </description>
